  "problem": "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0,3)=-9,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y,z)=y,\\,{f}_{y}(x,y,z)=x,\\,{f}_{z}(x,y,z)=-2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,0,3),$ estimate the value of $f(0.98,-0.01,3.1).$",
